          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/supreme-court-election-commission-form-6-sir-special-intensive-revision-of-electoral-rolls-logical-discrepancy-notices-101793233435159.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "The Supreme Court stated it had not upheld the Election Commission's 'logical discrepancy' classification, which previously led to the disenfranchisement of 2.71 million people in West Bengal.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/supreme-court-election-commission-form-6-sir-special-intensive-revision-of-electoral-rolls-logical-discrepancy-notices-101793233435159.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "Out of approximately 14.5 million electors at the start of Delhi's Special Intensive Revision, around 4.7 million did not submit enumeration forms.",
